center]4]<b>Explore the Perfect Tokyo Itinerary you Can’t Miss!</b> 

center]Check the full guide here: https://itimaker.com/blog/tokyo-itinerary 

Japan’s capital seamlessly blends historic sanctuaries with futuristic skyscrapers, offering an remarkable escape in the next season. Use our expert-crafted five-day schedule to maximize your stay. 

]Day 1 – Temples, Parks &amp; Skytree 
Begin at Tokyo’s oldest Senso-ji, saunter Nakamise Street for street bites, then relax in leafy Ueno Park. Cap the evening atop the 634 m Skytree for 360-degree views. 

]Day 2 – Culinary Delights &amp; Local Markets 
Kick off at Tsukiji Outer Market to indulge in tamago sando. Hop over to Harajuku for kawaii culture. 

]Culture Trip – Ueno to Ginza 
Immerse yourself in Tokyo National Museum, then window-shop in the chic Ginza district. Finish with Mori Art Museum for a art-filled finale. 

]Day 4 – Palaces &amp; Panoramas 
Wander the Imperial Palace grounds, record reels at picturesque arches, then ascend the iconic orange lattice for breathtaking cityscapes. 

]Day 5 – Relaxation &amp; Cultural Immersion 
Wind down with an onsen soak in bayside Odaiba, practice a chanoyu ritual, and peruse heritage streets of Yanaka before you head home. 

